      "side": 1,
      "message": "TableField has a parameter (TableInfo) in that allows for additional information of the table format. The parameters to that would be and interface/struct and the size of a row.\n\nDid not take it much further than that but the idea was to to provide pre-decoded rows (or rows for encoding) to be handled by the library.  Still a possibility.  So think of all the crazy table structs like the in EVTO ME or something as simple as  3 fields in this 5 byte row.  This size can help out in creating code that stores rows as individual byte slices or helping out in automating get-next logic should you be writing the ONU side of an OMCI conversation. \n\nI have a private project that implements this but have not had the time to create a generic way to pull in custom tableInfo structs to make use of it.",
